  "notes": "**Warmer and more consonant than the Premier/Havoc axis** — the research says so directly, and it is the parameter that separates this from everything else in the batch. Jazz minor with major-7th and 9th colour, `ii–V–i` and `i–VI–ii–V` over 2–4 bar loops with **genuine changes**, so `maxChords` is 4, `chordToneBias` is the highest here, and the extensions are seventh-dominant. Three researched drum facts are authored literally: **noticeably swung 8th hats** (`swing.amount` 0.62, the heaviest in this batch), **a ghost snare on the 16th before beat 3** — which is the `2a` slot, authored as a single high-probability ghost position rather than the genre's four — and a **tambourine layered in hooks**, which is the whole `percs` set. The bass is the reason this entry exists as a producer model rather than a variant: **sampled walking bass, prominent, playing 3rds and 5ths**, one of the more melodic bass departments in the lane, so `independent_riff` at 0.40, `cellShapes` built from the root, third and fifth the research names, and a register that reaches up to the chords' floor. Rhodes and vibes voicings sit mid-register with **a horn answer at bar ends**, which is `structure: question_answer` and an `answer_lick`-weighted counter. ⚠ `medium` and the research says why: credits and catalog are well documented, but **the workflow interviews are less technical than his peers'** — so the hat density, the open hat and the roll numbers are INFERRED.",
